# What "docker build" sends to the builder (the "build context").
#
# This file works the other way round from most ignore files. It ignores
# EVERYTHING first, and then names the few things the build needs. The
# reasons:
#
#   1. The image needs very little: the Go sources and one config file.
#      The old list left out a few things, but still sent docs, scripts,
#      schemas, tests, and local scratch directories.
#   2. A file that nobody thought of can never slip in. That matters for
#      secrets (.env.local, a key file): "COPY . ." in the Dockerfile would
#      put them in a builder layer.
#   3. Editing a doc or a script no longer throws away the build cache.
#
# The price: a NEW top-level Go package directory must be added below. If
# it is forgotten, "docker build" stops with a "package ... is not in std"
# error. It cannot go wrong quietly.
#
# The old list was: .git, .github, bin/, data/, coverage.out, *.test,
# *.out, .env. All of these are still left out, by the "*" line.

# 1. Ignore everything.
*

# 2. Let in what the Dockerfile uses.
#    Module files. The Dockerfile copies them first, to cache the downloads.
!go.mod
!go.sum
#    The default configuration. It is copied into the image as /app/gateway.yaml.
!gateway.yaml
#    The Go packages that ./cmd/scintx is built from.
!api
!cmd
!internal

# 3. Inside those directories, leave out what "go build" never reads.
#    These lines must stay AFTER the "!" lines: the last matching line wins.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
